Q: Navigation bar SwiftUI toolbar background A: <p>If you add a tiny amount of top padding to the <code>NavigationStack</code> then this breaks the contact with the safe area inset. The toolbar background then won't extend to the top of the screen.</p>
<ul>
<li><p>The padding only needs to be the size of 1 pixel. The environment value <code>pixelLength</code> can be used to get this size in points.</p>
</li>
<li><p>You probably don't want to add any padding if there is no top area inset. This may be the case on devices in landscape orientation. A <code>GeometryReader</code> can be used to measure the inset size.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<pre class="lang-swift prettyprint-override"><code>struct ContentView: View {
    @Environment(\.pixelLength) private var pixelLength

    var body: some View {
        GeometryReader { proxy in
            NavigationStack {
                Text(&quot;hello&quot;)
                    .navigationTitle(&quot;Working with GET request&quot;)
                    .navigationBarTitleDisplayMode(.inline)
                    .toolbarBackground(.yellow)
                    .toolbarBackground(.visible, for: .navigationBar)
            }
            .padding(.top, proxy.safeAreaInsets.top &gt; 0 ? pixelLength : 0)
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/Ei3TKTZP.png" alt="Screenshot" /></p>

Q: From a vector of structs, get a vector that collects one of the fields for every struct A: <p>You can use <a href="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/algorithm/transform" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>std::transform</code></a> and <a href="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/iterator/back_inserter" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>std::back_inserter</code></a> for that.</p>
<pre><code>std::vector&lt;Point&gt; pv;
pv.push_back(Point{1.0, 2.0,  3.0});
pv.push_back(Point{1.1, 0.0, -0.5});

std::vector&lt;double&gt; dv;

std::transform(pv.begin(), pv.end(), std::back_inserter(dv),
               [](Point const&amp; p) -&gt; double { return p.x; });
</code></pre>
